// bionic_shim.cpp -- runtime helpers used by translated dylibs.
//
// This file builds into libmacapk-bionic-shim.dylib. The translator
// links each translated APK .so dylib against this shim, so dyld
// auto-loads the shim alongside the translated dylib and resolves the
// extern symbols the translation phase couldn't fold in (calls to
// imported Bionic functions, Linux syscalls, and the lenient-mode
// panic stub for unsupported instructions).
//
// Stage 2 intentionally keeps the shim tiny. Each entry either:
//   - calls into libSystem directly when the Bionic ABI matches,
//   - logs and returns a sensible fallback when it doesn't,
//   - or aborts cleanly with a precise diagnostic when called from
//     a code path the translator couldn't safely model.
//
// As we run real APKs through the translator we expand the surface
// here, file by file, instead of writing per-app shims.

