// (`bl 0xf11ec34` = 0x9584c613). The queues are all (Manual,Manual) so nothing runs until someone
// calls XTaskQueueDispatch; MCPE's per-frame driver 0xad773ac does that and STOPS when MAIN blocks.
// This trap is the single choke point for EVERY XAL continuation submit -> it settles the deciding
// unknown (case a: the GS-issue hop is NEVER submitted -> upstream coroutine bug, XTaskQueue is
// irrelevant; case b: it IS submitted but never dispatched -> the fix is a serial host pump on the
// exact (queue,port) seen here). At the trap: x0=queue, w1=port(0 Work/1 Completion), w2=delayMs,
// x3=runnable ctx, [x3]=vtable (logged as a file-vaddr so a submit can be identified by type).
// LOG-ONLY: it emulates the `bl` (lr=pc+4, pc=submit target) so the real submit still happens.
// REMOVAL CONDITION: delete once case a/b is settled and the real fix lands. Gated default-OFF.
static uintptr_t g_xsubmit_trace_addr = 0;
static std::atomic<int> g_xsubmit_hits{0};

// ---- XAL submit-queue pump (MACAPK_XSUBMIT_PUMP) — THE MCPE 54%-STALL FIX (v655) ----------------
// Live-proven root cause (v655 xsubmit trace at mc+0x8fed3e8): the sign-in auth chain posts every
// continuation via XTaskQueueSubmitDelayedCallback to (Manual,Manual) XTaskQueues. In a stall run the
// chain emits exactly 14 submits in a ~2s burst, and the LAST hops (the post-HTTP continuations,
// vt@0x13473c88) land on the MAIN auth queue's WORK port -- posted from an OkHttp worker, NOT MAIN.
// The ONLY dispatcher of a Manual queue is MCPE's per-frame driver 0xad773ac, which runs on MINECRAFT
// MAIN's game loop; by then MAIN has parked in the sign-in wait 0x11ee7440 and stopped iterating
// frames -> the continuation strands in the queue forever -> the coroutine never reaches the
// GatheringService request -> permanent 54% freeze. (~40% cross = MAIN dispatches the queue in the
// race window before it enters the blocking wait.) Fable a9303af2 independently confirmed this is a
// drainer-liveness race, not a lost wake. THE FIX: a dedicated host thread (x18-preserved + JVM-
// attached, so it can run guest coroutine code) that keeps dispatching BOTH ports of every XTaskQueue
// captured at the submit choke point, so the auth chain advances OFF-MAIN while MAIN is parked.
// XTaskQueueDispatch(q,port,0) pops one item from a lock-free LocklessQueue (safe concurrent with the
// driver); a single host thread = serial, so the coroutine transition (mutex-guarded) is never
// touched by two threads at once. Gated MACAPK_XSUBMIT_PUMP, default OFF (default MCPE path unchanged).
