    // docs/pairip-mapfiles-fold-80vs5. +0x33698 `csel w8,w11,w9,lo` (word 0x1a893168): idx<0x5e(94) ->
    // w11=0x b1c595ff (CONTINUE the tail 10cdda24 loop), idx>=0x5e -> w9=0x497096df (EXIT). Ours EXITs at
    // iteration 66 (idx=98); the device CONTINUEs to 144. This forces CONTINUE (up to K times) while the
    // dispatch counter is in [lo,hi], to test whether running the tail loop to ~144 moves the +0x440c4
