// CallStaticIntMethodV / ...A (vtable slots 130 / 131, offsets 0x208 / 0x20c).
//
// BOTH WERE DISPATCHED TO THE NON-V HANDLER until v1.0.805, and it was a silent
// wrong-answer bug rather than a crash. The non-V forwarder takes the FIRST
// VARIADIC ARG in r3 (ARM32 AAPCS: env r0, clazz r1, methodID r2, arg0 r3); the
// V form instead puts a POINTER TO A va_list there, and the A form a jvalue[]
// pointer. So every CallStaticIntMethodV read the va_list pointer itself as if
// it were the first integer argument.
